A||||11||G25C||Gas guage always says "full"
Z||000000||G25C||07-22-99||10:36 PM||||<br>I never had a problem with my gas guage untill today.  I was driving down a smooth back road cruzing at 80.  As i slowed down for a curve the gas guage needle wavered from Full to half and then went up to Full and stayed there.  Its still there and hasnt moved.  And i know the tank wasnt full. (infact i stopped for gas and it took 9 gallons to fill it up...).<p>Anyone know why it did this?  Is this something easy to fix?<p>what would miles per gallon be under normall driving distances, So i can kinda watch the odometer to know when i gettng low on fuel.<p>  I live out in the country and i dont do a lot of stop and go driving, mostly highway.
Z||000001||batboy||07-22-99||11:46 PM||||...your mileage may vary...<p>Ever hear those words, well they're true. My 4 cylinder Fiero gets over 300 miles to the tank full. To play it really safe, if I were you, I'd fill up about every 200 miles.
Z||000002||JetroGT||07-23-99||12:58 AM||||It could be the float in the tank or corsion on some of the connectors going to the gauge cluster. If you have an extra set of gauges, try swapping them.
Z||000003||theogre||07-23-99||07:47 AM||||likely shorted the wire to the sender. the wire is probly rubbed thru some place under the car. The tank shifts a bit in it's mounts. If the wire is tight/pinched the tank can wear thru the insulation.
Z||000004||ChadMan||07-23-99||07:50 AM||||batboy, your mileage is amazing!  I have to fill up the V6 at 200 miles and the 4-banger at 240.  Neither car will take more than 8.5 gallons, even though the 88 is supposed to have an 11.5 gallon tank.
Z||000005||Formula||07-23-99||08:54 AM||||My gas gauge is always on empty. I put 5 bucks of gas in it every 100 miles. (its usually $5.25) This morning I put $12.25 in it and it nevwer clicked off.......I wonder how big my gas tank is?
Z||000006||G25C||07-23-99||09:01 AM||||I'll think i'll fill up around 150 miles just to be safe, and i'll check over the other things mentioned.  Incidently, once my gas guage read 1/4 tank and then it stalled cause it was actualy out of gas.  I read on the internet how to fix that problem, but required dropping the tank and i didnt want to do it if i didnt have to (guess maybe now i do?).<p>I got maybe a gallon of gas off some guy and it was enough to make it home. (i was only 2 miles away when it ran out).<p>The next day i drove to the gas station and it took about 11 gallons to fill up the tank.  My fiero is a 87 GT.
Z||000007||batboy||07-23-99||06:49 PM||||ChadMan, I average about 32-34 mpg with my 4 cylinder, but nearly all my driving is on the open highway, most of which is posted 55 mph (I usually do about 60). If I'm driving 70-75 mph on the interstate or doing more city driving, obviously my mileage drops considerably.
Z||000008||Linx||07-23-99||10:13 PM||||Wow- i had this same problem and fixed it a month ago.  The "sensor" in the tank was bad.  It's a resistive element- or basically, a wire wound resistor attached to the float.  The element had opened (the wire broke).  I couldnt get the element; it's part of the fuel pump assy. and it's an all-or-nothing part, Im told.  In a moment of brilliance, I repaired the element and reassembled it.  I was so impressed with my fix that I started on a page to submit to my fave fiero web-hangouts;<br>http://members.aol.com/linxramblr/fix.html
